,"weight":0.25},"balance_sheet":{"score":0.086,"weight":0.2},"value_destruction":{"score":0.678,"weight":0.2},"derating":{"score":0.243,"weight":0.15},"market":{"score":0.191,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 7% operating margin is roughly in line with the Consumer Defensive median (7%).","It earns less of the sector's profit than its revenue share would suggest (0.92x).","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+10.2% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.07 across 172 companies in the universe; the top four hold 38% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 51% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 25% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 39% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 46% and a beta of 0.86, it moves roughly with the market, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.12 vs 5y 0.69), so read it loosely.","About $10.1M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 30% in the 2020 crash, 66% in the 2022 bear market and 36% in 2008."],"val":["The stock trades 19% below its DCF fair value of $45.76, a meaningful margin of safety.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 32%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $36.14 to $59.56 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks cheap against Consumer Defensive peers: EV/EBITDA 7.5 vs 10.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 4% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are mixed: an FCF yield of 6.8% (above the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 7.6% (vs the 8% bar).","The 6 covering analysts target $62.00 on average, 66% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 5% falls short of the cost of capital of 8.8%, so growth at these returns destroys value; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 1.63).","It converts 7% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: cash conversion of 1.96x.","ROE of 11% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.8x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.3% of revenue on stock compensation."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $79.4M (12% of market cap).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.46)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 2.3% over 3 years, 15.1% over 5 years and 7.1% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","At current returns, reinvesting 9% of profits supports about 0.4% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 2.9% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Margins are contracting (-1.2% trend).","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.0x, 2.4% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 21, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 5.0%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (8 sales, net $1.3M sold).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.6% (0.6% in buybacks).","Short interest is elevated at 15.7% of the float, 9.6 days to cover."],"people":["With about 2,360 employees, each generates about $275K of revenue, 0.5x the Consumer Defensive median, and productivity has risen 9.6% a year.","That works out to $20K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.0M (7x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $4K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":72,"head":"Watch: LEAN BUY-rated, but it earns less than its cost of capital.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 43, gates 10/26)","Trades 19% below fair value of $45.76","Revenue grew 15.1%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $79.4M","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["ROIC 4.9% vs WACC 8.8%","Operating margin contracting 1.2%/yr"],"flags":[],"need":["it earns less than its cost of capital"],"buy_below":38.9,"vc":{"base":45.76,"base_src":"dcf","bear":36.14,"bull":59.56,"alt_median":17.8,"n_alt":2,"gap":1.5702,"dispersion":0.3201,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (32% dispersion)","DCF is 157% above the other models' median ($17.80)"]},"med":{"pe":18.5188,"ev_ebitda":10.2635,"pfcf":15.9681,"pb":2.0792,"roic":0.1185,"gross_margin":0.3401,"fcf_margin":0.0601,"div_yield":0.0296}},"ticker":"APEI","date":"2026-11-06"}